heme":"Infrastructure, Construction & Real Estate","tier":"2"},{"status":"Runner-up","subtheme":"Bearings & motion-control localization","tag":"Bearings","theme":"Industrials & Capital Goods","tier":"1"}],"thesis":"Goodluck is mid-transformation from a commodity steel-products maker into a diversified engineering-solutions player, deliberately shifting mix toward high-margin value-added products (front fork tubes, GI conduit pipes for US export, hydraulic tubes) and a new defence vertical (heavy-caliber artillery shells via Goodluck Defence & Aerospace). FY26 showed the thesis working at the margin line — EBITDA grew ~21-26% on only ~3-4% revenue growth (strong operating leverage / mix), gross margin moved from ~27-28% to ~33% YoY, and PAT margin improved. The optionality is the defence ramp (FY27 defence revenue guided INR250-300 cr from INR46 cr in FY26) and a planned 4-lakh-shell capacity. Near-term overhang: West Asia war disrupting logistics/exports, soft steel prices capping topline, and elevated working capital / net debt (~INR1,000 cr).","trig":[]},"lm":"2026-06","m":4763,"mem":1,"pdd":"2023-10-31","prev_stage":3,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":198.1,"s":"GOODLUCK","sig":"Advancing (S2)","sx":{"SMA_50":"488.4","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":"","pct_below_52w_high":"14.0","pct_change_from_prev_signal":"","pivot_close":"","pivot_low":"","stage_changed_since_prev_signal":"","vpe_df_60d_sum":"1.1","vpe_zone_cumul_df":"0.5"},"t":""}},"s":"GOODLUCK"}